Ported from the TypeScript build's __tests__/cases/rust/026-happy-do-not-scan-past-leading-doc-comment.case.yaml; expected output is the TypeScript build's, except:
- The `//!` comment is the header comment; the TypeScript build read only `//` lines and gave no header here.
- Signatures print as written on one line (`fn main()`, not `fn main ()`), with generics, a const's or static's type, and a type alias's type; the TypeScript build printed keyword and name only, spaced out.
== args
input/doc-comment-before-regular-comment.rs
== file input/doc-comment-before-regular-comment.rs
//! Module docs stay excluded.
// Regular comment should not be treated as file header in this case.
fn main() {}
== stdout
input/doc-comment-before-regular-comment.rs
Module docs stay excluded.
[L3-L3] fn main()
